%I A399884 #16 Sep 21 2026 17:15:15
%S A399884 0,1,2,75
%N A399884 Variant of the Busy Beaver sequence for the Post correspondence problem.
%C A399884 Let PCP[n] be the set of Post correspondence problem (PCP) instances consisting of at most n dominoes (i.e., at most n pairs of nonempty strings) over the binary alphabet {0,1}, such that the maximum width of the strings in the dominoes is n. The length of a solution for a PCP instance is the number of dominoes (repetitions are allowed). a(n) = the maximum of the lengths of the shortest solutions of the instances in PCP[n].
%C A399884 The Post correspondence problem (PCP) is undecidable, and this sequence is noncomputable.
%C A399884 Confirmation that a(2) is 2 can be found in Zhao's paper (link below).
%C A399884 Confirmation that a(3) is 75 can be found in Rahn's doctoral thesis and Zhao's paper (links below).
%C A399884 Confirmation that a(4) >= 781 can be found on page 350 of the Goodman-Strauss paper (link below).
%D A399884 E.L. Post, A variant of a recursively unsolvable problem, Bulletin of the American Mathematical Society, 52, 264-268, 1946.
%H A399884 Chaim Goodman-Strauss, <a href="http://www.ams.org/notices/201003/rtx100300343p.pdf">Can’t Decide? Undecide!</a>, Notices of the AMS, Volume 57, Number 3, pp. 343-356, March 2010.
%H A399884 Turlough Neary, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6700">Undecidability in binary tag systems and the Post correspondence problem for four pairs of words</a>, arXiv:1312.6700 [cs.FL], 2013.
%H A399884 OeisWiki, <a href="https://oeis.org/wiki/Busy_Beaver_numbers">Busy Beaver numbers</a>.
%H A399884 Mirko Rahn, <a href="https://publikationen.bibliothek.kit.edu/1000009979">Entscheidbare Fälle des Postschen Korrespondenzproblems</a>, Doctoral Thesis, Universität Fridericiana zu Karlsruhe, 2008.
%H A399884 Mirko Rahn, <a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0020019007003031">More decidable instances of Post’s correspondence problem: beyond counting</a>, Information Processing Letters, Volume 106, Issue 3, 2008, Pages 115-119.
%H A399884 Heiko Stamer, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090415224613/http://www.theory.informatik.uni-kassel.de/~stamer/pcp/pcpcontest_en.html">Welcome to PCP@HOME!</a>.
%H A399884 Thomas, <a href="https://mathoverflow.net/questions/358201/post-correspondence-problem-busy-beaver-variant">Post correspondence problem: Busy beaver variant</a>.
%H A399884 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/BusyBeaver.html">Busy Beaver</a>.
%H A399884 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Busy_beaver">Busy beaver</a>.
%H A399884 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post_correspondence_problem">Post correspondence problem</a>.
%H A399884 Ling Zhao, <a href="https://webdocs.cs.ualberta.ca/~games/PCP/paper/CG2002.pdf">Tackling Post’s Correspondence Problem</a>, University of Alberta, Last revised on Apr 25 2003.
%H A399884 <a href="/index/Br#beaver">Index entries for sequences related to Busy Beaver problem</a>.
%F A399884 a(n+1) >= a(n).
%Y A399884 Cf. A028444, A060843, A309250.
